Icon sets in this folder

These are the built-in sets the Inbox offers for agents' icons ("Sets" in the face picker). Each folder holds one
set: manifest.json (names, numbers, search words) and icons.bin (the icons' bytes, one after the other; built by
scripts/build-icon-sets.ts). The server embeds both in the binary and serves one icon at a time when a window asks.
They are not covered by this repository's MIT or Apache license; each set's own terms follow.

game-icons/ (game-icons.net creatures, 334 icons)
  Icons made by Delapouite, Lorc, Caro Asercion, Skoll, Cathelineau, Carl Olsen, DarkZaitzev, Faithtoken, Sparker.
  Available on https://game-icons.net. Licensed under CC BY 3.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/).
  The "Various artists" icon (Salmon) is CC0. Changes: the black background square removed and the fill set to
  the theme's text colour. Per-author list: game-icons/CREDITS.md (the Inbox serves it from the picker's credits
  line). Upstream terms: game-icons/UPSTREAM-LICENSE.txt.

tiny-creatures/ (Tiny Creatures, 170 icons)
  Tiny Creatures by Clint Bellanger (clintbellanger.net), CC0 1.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/). No credit required; given as a courtesy.
  Upstream terms: tiny-creatures/UPSTREAM-LICENSE.txt.

dcss/ (Dungeon Crawl, 419 icons)
  Dungeon Crawl Stone Soup tiles, https://github.com/crawl/tiles (releases/Nov-2015/mon), CC0
  (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/). No credit required; given as a courtesy.

noto-3d/ (Noto Emoji 3D, 149 icons)
  From https://github.com/googlefonts/noto-emoji, folder 3D/png/128 (Google). The folder carries no licence file of
  its own; the repository's fonts are under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 and its README puts "most image
  resources" under Apache 2.0. Which licence covers the 3D PNGs is asked upstream in googlefonts/noto-emoji#592.
  Details, and how to remove or swap this set: noto-3d/LICENSE.md.

Names: the sets' display names and search words were written for Plannotator (Tiny Creatures ships none; the
others' come from their file names). Each folder's LICENSE.md says how its licence was established.
